{
  "name": "wallspace-taste-only",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "policyText": "Wallspace plans outdoor advertising by taste: the things people love (shows, music, food, hobbies, places). The company policy is taste only, never identity. Refuse any brief or copy line that targets, selects, excludes or describes people by: race or ethnicity; religion; sexual orientation; gender identity; disability or health condition; age used as an identity (age bands, generations, life-stage labels as a target); nationality or immigration status. Also refuse copy that makes a health claim (cures, treats, prevents, clinically proven, weight loss results) or a financial claim (guaranteed returns, get rich, earn money, no credit check, debt relief). Words that name a taste or a thing are fine: Black Friday sale, soul food, gospel brunch, Korean BBQ, Latin jazz, halal cart, black coffee, Christian rock, black comedy. When refusing, suggest the taste version: the same audience described by what they love.",
